// Rule: [T1204.002] Sourtrade - Browser Created Large Executable
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1204.002
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents
// Purpose: Hunting for oversized Windows executables created by browsers after in-page Bun assembly.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceFileEvents for browser created large executable using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result shows a supported browser creating an executable at least 600 MB in size.
// A match does not prove: This is consistent with the source-observed SourTrade delivery shape but does not prove browser-side assembly, malicious bytecode, execution, credential theft, or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// SourTrade browser-created oversized executable
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: DeviceFileEvents from Microsoft Defender for Endpoint
//
// Source evidence:
// - SourTrade uses a browser SharedWorker to assemble a Windows executable.
// - The published /config sample specifies a 665,136,399-byte AES-CTR stream.
// - A ServiceWorker returns the assembled stream as a same-origin attachment.
//
// The 600,000,000-byte threshold is intentionally below the source-observed
// random component. It is campaign-oriented hunting logic, not a general
// malicious-file threshold and not a production alert.
DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType == "FileCreated"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ (
    "chrome.exe",
    "msedge.exe",
    "firefox.exe",
    "brave.exe",
    "opera.exe"
)
| where FileName endswith ".exe"
| where FileSize >= 600000000
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    FileSize,
    SHA1,
    FileOriginUrl,
    FileOriginReferrerUrl,
    FileOriginIP,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc

// Interpretation:
// A result shows a supported browser creating an executable at least 600 MB
// in size. This is consistent with the source-observed SourTrade delivery
// shape but does not prove browser-side assembly, malicious bytecode, execution,
// credential theft, or attribution.
//
// Validate:
// 1. Confirm FileSize and FileOrigin* population for browser downloads.
// 2. Inspect Mark of the Web, PE sections, signer metadata, and the .bun section.
// 3. Baseline legitimate large browser-delivered installers and developer tools.
// 4. Correlate manually with execution, network activity, and user intent.
